  "about": "The franchise ruling the team pages read: every team code of the day in the ledger (the REST's teamAbbrev) mapped to the current franchise whose statistical history it is part of, or to null for a franchise that no longer plays (defunct, or inactive). It follows the NHL's own ruling, which can change: on 2026-09-24 the NHL gave the Winnipeg Jets the Jets' 1979-96 seasons and the Atlanta Thrashers' (1999-2011), left the inactive Coyotes Phoenix and Arizona (1996-2024) only, and gave Utah (2024) no inherited history. To re-rule, edit `codes` (and `version`) and rebuild; src/lib/groups.ts reads this file and nothing else. A code is unique to its era in this ledger (WIN is the first Jets, WPG the second; SEN the first Senators, OTT the second), so no code needs a season range yet; if one ever does, add it to `ranges` as {code, from, to, franchise}, which wins over `codes` for those seasons.",
